Package: qmi-supervisor
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Anthony Pogo <anthony1997@hotmail.es>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-qmi-1.0, libqmi-utils, libqmi-proxy, iproute2, udev, kmod
Recommends: udhcpc, resolvconf, gpsd
Suggests: iperf3
Homepage: https://github.com/ANTS-research-group/qmi-supervisor
Description: QMI supervisor for USB modems with web interface
 Supervises autoconnect and telemetry for one or more USB QMI modems, with an
 optional web interface served from a static export.
 .
 It provides per-modem profiles, connection verification, routing policy,
 daily CSV/JSON captures and GPS support. The systemd unit runs a process
 manager that starts only the children each modem profile needs.
 .
 This package installs the application in /opt/qmi-supervisor and keeps the
 configuration in /etc/qmi-supervisor.ini and the captures in
 /var/lib/qmi-supervisor, so upgrades preserve both. The first installation
 enables the web interface with a generated admin password printed once. Host
 policy that affects other managers (ModemManager, NetworkManager) remains an
 explicit qmi-supervisor-configure decision.
